WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.015 --> 00:00:06.133
Your world in Mimir: every entry in one library, with its art.

2
00:00:06.333 --> 00:00:12.557
Open an entry: structured fields, classes and stats, and every link.

3
00:00:12.757 --> 00:00:19.171
The family tree draws itself from the relationships on each entry.

4
00:00:19.371 --> 00:00:25.900
Maps hold pins that link straight back to entries.

5
00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:33.361
The timeline runs on the world's own calendar.

6
00:00:33.561 --> 00:00:39.581
Plan a story as beats, each with its art and its consequence.

7
00:00:39.781 --> 00:00:45.615
Test a quest: play it through and choose at each branch.

8
00:00:45.815 --> 00:00:52.258
The run ends with its outcome and the paths it never reached.

9
00:00:52.458 --> 00:00:57.541
Running a game? Decide what each player and group can know.

10
00:00:57.741 --> 00:01:03.504
Then see exactly what one player sees, and what is withheld.

11
00:01:03.704 --> 00:01:08.755
Ask Mimir about your own world. It reads only your entries.

12
00:01:08.955 --> 00:01:18.442
First it shows what matched, so you can remove what is not relevant.

13
00:01:18.642 --> 00:01:25.066
Every change is kept in history. Open any version and restore it.

14
00:01:25.266 --> 00:01:28.267
Your world, in readable files that stay yours.
